<title>JAPAN: Japan 96/97 first half trade surplus down 41.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan 96/97 first half trade surplus down 41.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's customs-cleared trade surplus in the first six months of 1996/97 fell 41.6 percent from the same period a year earlier to 2.90 trillion yen, the Finance Ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>Japan's merchandise trade surplus with the United States, often a source of friction between the two countries, declined 24.2 percent to 1.56 trillion yen in the April-September period from a year earlier. The figures were not adjusted for seasonal factors.</p>
